    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d427">

                <pb facs="0494" n="476" sameAs="frus:frus1946v11/pg476"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.796/8–246: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Pawley</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">restricted</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-08-12T18:00:00-04:00">August 12, 1946—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1081. CAA unenthusiastic over Brazilian proposed
                    technical assistance agreement but will probably await Tippett arrival before
                    recommending changes to Dept. Dept. suggests advisability at Emb discretion <pb facs="0495" n="477"
                        xml:id="pg477"/> of deferring conclusion civil aviation technical assistance
                    pending outcome bilateral transport negotiations.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
